>> title: Sicilian Pan Dough
>> category: Breads
>> tags: bread, pizza, dough, yeast, italian, high hydration
>> counters: Pizzeria
>> aka: sicilian dough, square pizza dough, pan pizza dough, tray dough, sicilian pizza dough
>> pairs-with: sicilian-pizza
>> servings: 12
>> time: 5 hr
>> slack: forgiving — it will not be pressed out cold, because a chilled dough fights back and tears rather than filling the pan

>> step: mix to a wet, shaggy dough
Mix @bread flour{4 1/4%cup}(600 g), @instant yeast{1 1/2%tsp}(5 g), @fine sea salt{1%Tbs}(14 g), @warm water{2%cup}(450 g) and @extra-virgin olive oil{2%Tbs}(30 mL) in a #bowl{} to a wet, shaggy dough that will not hold a shape.

>> step: fold four times over 2 hr
Fold @&(~1)dough{} over on itself four times with a wet hand, a half hour apart, ~rise{2%hr} in all.

>> step: press into an oiled tray
Press @&(~1)risen dough{} into a #12x16-in pan{} slicked with @olive oil{3%Tbs}(45 mL), pushing it out from the middle towards the corners.

>> step: prove 2 hr, until it fills the corners
Prove @&(~1)dough{} covered ~prove{2%hr}, until it has filled the pan to the edges and wobbles when you shake the tray.

Press it out in two goes if it fights you. It cannot be halved into smaller trays so scale it whole.
